{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail\/color"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinedetail\/color"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLLineDetailV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"color"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineDetail/color":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail\/color","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinedetail\/color","abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"title":"color"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLineDetail":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLineDetail","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineDetail"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLineDetail"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllinedetail","abstract":[{"text":"If the staff-lines element is present, the appearance of each line may be individually specified with a line-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"detail type. Staff lines are numbered from bottom to top. The print-object attribute allows lines to be hidden","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within a staff. This is used in special situations such as a widely-spaced percussion staff where a note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"placed below the higher line is distinct from a note placed above the lower line. Hidden staff lines are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"included when specifying clef lines and determining display-step \/ display-octave values, but are not counted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as lines for the purposes of the system-layout and staff-layout elements.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLLineDetail"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"}}}